# Figure 6, second batch of seeds: vtag = 10..19 (40 runs), on top of the
# v0..v9 already trained by condor/fig6.sub and condor/fig6_seeds.sub. Takes
# the four synthv09082026 nets to twenty seeds each.
#
#   condor_submit_bid 100 condor/fig6_seeds2.sub
#
# NOTE: multiseed.SEEDS in src/analysis/RELEVANT/multiseed.py is range(10), so
# the *_multiseed figure scripts still average v0..v9 only. Widen SEEDS (or set
# it per script) to actually use these.
#
# vtag reseeds jax.random.PRNGKey only, i.e. the network INITIALISATION;
# load_dataset takes a deterministic 90/10 prefix split with no shuffling, so
# every seed sees identical data.
#
# Safe to resubmit: execute_don.py no-ops when the net directory already exists
# (execute_don.py:120), so completed runs are skipped rather than redone.
#
# ~200 s per run measured over the first twenty runs, so ~2.2 CPU-hours total.

initialdir   = /fast/jtaraz/MISC/ModeDecomposition-DeepONets
executable   = condor/train_one.sh
arguments    = $(args)
getenv       = True

output       = condor/logs/fig6_seeds2.$(ClusterId).$(ProcId).out
error        = condor/logs/fig6_seeds2.$(ClusterId).$(ProcId).err
log          = condor/logs/fig6_seeds2.$(ClusterId).$(ProcId).log

request_cpus   = 4
request_memory = 8192
request_disk   = 8192
request_gpus   = 0

queue args from condor/fig6_seeds2_args.txt
